dsv41 patch 0051 (20.10.2026): the indexer's weights_proj GEMV off the main stream's critical path.
Base: vllm/models/deepseek_v41/attention.py of image v5.
Why: in a profile of the decode round (1 stream) the main stream waited 50-105 us in each of the 8 indexer layers for
indexer.weights_proj (bf16 GEMV hidden -> 32 heads, cuBLAS with 2 CTAs, 56-61 us on GB10), 0.54 ms a round: the GEMV
runs on an aux stream next to fused_wqa_wkv, and the default stream joined it right after that GEMM, although its
result is first read by fused_indexer_q_rope_quant much later. In the short-context case forward() selects every
candidate and never reads the weights (TensorFold skips the GEMV there too).
How: the join moves to the read (right before fused_indexer_q_rope_quant); with short contexts the GEMV is not
launched. Same kernels, same inputs: bit-identical.
Measured (20.10.2026, GB10, 2000 MHz, image v6): only on top of patch 0054, against 0054 alone: geometric mean +0.2 %
(-1.50 against -1.70 % relative to neither), inside the run-to-run spread. Not adopted.
Switch: VLLM_DSV41_INDEXER_DEFER=1 (default 0 = off).

